Short : HD-Installer for Alien Breed 3D Enhanced
Type : game/patch
Author : Psygore (psygore@whdload.de), Vesuri (version 2.0b)


Alien Breed 3D Enhanced 2.0b (26.11.2026)
Original install: Psygore. Version 2.0b improvements: Vesuri.

That install applies to "Alien Breed 3D" © 1995 Team 17
It supports floppy disks, CD32 and aminet (8ch sound patch) version.

It requires:
 - WHDLoad 18+
 - 732 KB ChipMem (584 KB without music) & 2.0 MB OtherMem (+2.0 MB extra
   mem for preload)
 - AGA chipset and a 68020 processor (at least)
 - XFD package must be installed to depack some files
 - Enhanced resolution (CUSTOM5) runs on any 68020 or better; it is best
   on a 68030, or a 68020 card of 28 MHz or more. On a stock 14 MHz 68020
   the original display (without CUSTOM5) is two to three times as fast


Version 2.0b (26.11.2026) by Vesuri:
 - Enhanced resolution (CUSTOM5): the game is drawn at 1x1 pixels, 192x160
   in the small view and 288x240 in full screen, on 256-colour screens
   (the installed, the Aminet 8-channel and the CD32 version; not the
   floppy one)
 - the installed icon sets CUSTOM5=1; remove it for the original display
 - frames a second, small view / full screen (emulated): 6 / 4 on a 14 MHz
   68020, 11 / 8 at 28 MHz, 18 / 13 on a 50 MHz 68030, 20 / 11 on a 25 MHz
   68040 (the original display: 12, 19, 23 and 26)
 - fixed: the game could stop on a black screen before the menu (the
   no-music slave on a 28 MHz 68020), the Team 17 picture could show as
   garbage on a real A1200, the menu's fades had off colours and a frame of
   garbage could show on the way back to the menu
 - the slave's source is included, a reconstruction of Psygore's slave

Version 1.3 (08.01.2020) by Psygore:
 - An access fault removed (level 13), thanks to Angus for the bug report
   (mantis #4316)
 - CUSTOM1 for trainers modified, set
   CUSTOM1=1 for unlimited energy
   CUSTOM1=2 for unlimited shots
   CUSTOM1=4 to skip level
   To select unlimited energy and shots, set CUSTOM1=3 (1+2), ...  

Version 1.2 (05.04.2014) by Psygore:
 - Slave updated for WHDLoad 17+ (custom options displayed on splash window)
 - CPU caches was enabled before detecting CPU type (on 060, all caches were
   not enabled). This is fixed now.
 - Joystick control is set by default (as CD32 version)
 - If 'plain shaded' is selected with joypad for floor detail, pause option was
   broken. Fixed now.
 - Press 'Reverse+Forward+Play' (at least 1 sec. with joypad) to quit slave
 - Install script updated

Version 1.1 (25.06.2011) by Psygore:
 - Slave completely rewritten (no need OSEmu anymore)
 - CD32 version and joypad supported (thanks to Sascha Steinert)
 - Trainer added (CUSTOM1=1, unlimited energy and ammo, F1 to skip level)
 - Set CUSTOM2=1 for LMB=forward/RMB=fire (mouse control)
 - Set CUSTOM2=2 for RMB=forward/LMB=fire (mouse control)
 - Set CUSTOM3=1 to load aminet version (abd8ch)
 - Set CUSTOM4=1 to enable main music (HackAB3D) in the end part
 - Load/Save prefs file
 - All unpacked files (abd.pk, HackAB3D,...) can be packed as data with Propack
 - New install script
 - Some box icons added
 - The game must be re-installed

Version 1.0 (29.09.2001) by Psygore:
 - SSP & USP relocated to fast memory
 - OSEmu used (2nd copper-list is not reloaded)
 - Password protection removed
 - 'HackAB3D' supported (just copy it to 'data' dir)
 - Aminet version (8 ch sound patch) supported, depack 'abd.pk' with XFD
   and copy it to 'data' dir
 - Access fault removed
 - Quit with F10


Note:
This slave needs less memory than the original game now (a slave -no music- is
included, only 428kb (!) chipmem required, HackAB3D will not be loaded).
The access fault which occured in the version 1.0 is caused by a random read
(outside a data table in the game code), this is fixed now. And some problems
you may have had with ennemies and objects should be removed.

You can download the 8ch sound patch here:
http://aminet.net/game/patch/AB3D-patch.lha
Depack the file, rename it to adb8ch and copy it in data/ dir.
Use CUSTOM3=1 option to load it. Just notice there is no end part in this
version.

and the music here:
ftp://ftp.team17.com/pub/t17/goodies/hackab3d.lha
Depack the archive and copy the file into data/ dir.

Known bug: if you use 'HackAB3D' and the aminet version, when you go back
           to the main screen, the music is corrupted.
This bug is removed from slave 1.1.

Thanks go to Bored Seal for sending the disk-files and for testing it!


